{
  "_provenance": {
    "version": "1.8",
    "protocol": 47,
    "mapping_source": "mcp-community",
    "kind": "curated-legacy",
    "note": "1.8 has no VoxelShape API; meta-0 collision boxes read per block from the deobfuscated vanilla 1.8.9 tree (net.minecraft.block.*), cross-checked against the obfuscated 1.8.4 server. Non-listed ids default to full cube in DataGen legacy mode.",
    "meta_supplement": "collision_by_block_state lists only the (id << 4 | meta) states whose collision differs from their block's meta-0 shape in collision_by_block_id; every other state inherits it. Derived by tools/extraction/add_legacy_meta_shapes.py from vanilla's own getStateFromMeta and bounding-box code, using each band's own meta-0 box so per-band geometry is preserved.",
    "omitted": "Ids left unlisted keep DataGen's documented legacy default of a full cube. That is deliberate for the connection-geometry families, whose real box needs neighbours the pre-flattening wire does not carry: fence (85, 113, 188-192), cobblestone_wall (139), iron_bars (101), glass_pane (102), stained_glass_pane (160). A cube over-blocks rather than under-blocks there, which is the conservative direction. minecraft:farmland (60) is unlisted for a different reason: 1.8's BlockFarmland.getCollisionBoundingBox returns the WHOLE cube even though its render bounds stop at 0.9375, so a full cube is not a fallback there, it is correct. The 0.9375 farmland collision arrives at 1.9. minecraft:cocoa (127) and minecraft:piston_head (34) are omitted rather than guessed: cocoa's box moves on three axes with age and facing and has no family rule, and 1.8's BlockPistonExtension.applyCoreBounds keeps the arm INSIDE the block (DOWN is 0.375,0.25,0.375 -> 0.625,1,0.625) where the shared piston_head family models 1.12's arm reaching a whole block out, so applying that rule here would invent geometry."
  },
